"""Summarise the complete selected source cohort; keep acceptance gaps explicit."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def main():
    cohort=json.loads((ROOT/'artefacts/data/ds10-action-console-19-2026-10-12.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
    report=json.loads((ROOT/'artefacts/data/ds10-automated-session-proposals-2026-10-12.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
    distinct=len(report['distinct_session_proposals']);rows=sum(len(r['seed_sessions']) for r in cohort['records'])
    lines=['# DS-10 selected-source completion report — 12 October 2026','','Owner: **Imran Tajuddin**. Delivery: draft PR #71; acceptance ticket #39.','','## Outcome',f'All **19 selected records** now have extraction or an explicit source-review outcome: 11 aggregate programmes, six route recoveries, one place conversion and one mobile-service review. There are **{distinct} distinct unapproved proposals**, represented by **{rows} parent rows** in the action console. The difference is shared Hertfordshire Story Time rows and mixed Cambridge Storytime/Rhymetime identities. **Eleven Shredder rows are enquiry-only coach/day drafts, not timed sessions.**','','This report completes the requested source pass. It does not close #39, claim the broader 191-record queue is approved, or establish pilot coverage. Sources already extracting well were preserved rather than re-audited. No live database writes, source activation, canonical venue creation, merge or deployment occurred in this source-proposal work. Earlier historical corrections documented on #39 remain a separate live batch.','','## Programme results','','| Parent programme | Proposed rows | Qualification / remaining work |','|---|---:|---|']
    for r in cohort['records']:
        if r['group']=='split' or r['title']=='Baby Gym':
            a=r.get('automation',{});status='Reviewed page scope complete; owner and venue checks remain' if a.get('coverage_complete') else 'Partial / further source or owner evidence required'
            if r['title']=='Shredder Skate School':status='Coach/day drafts only; published clock times and availability missing'
            lines.append('| '+r['title']+' | '+str(len(r['seed_sessions']))+' | '+status+' |')
    lines+=['','Library.Live Rhymetime: 33 detail pages reviewed, 31 retained proposals; two relocated listings excluded and Huntingdon addresses unresolved. Storytime: 16 detail pages, two shared Rhymetime identities; six flags across five listings. Both council programmes support offline snapshot parsing only: provider robots disallows unattended collection. A permitted feed or authorised route remains required.','','GK Fit: 11 proposals from 19 catalogue cards; eight ended/full cards excluded. Course start labels and term lengths are not expanded into invented occurrences. Royston Nov–Dec card times supersede older timetable times; year/end bounds remain unknown. Holiday regularity requires classification review.','','Scouts: 51 proposals across 16 of 21 groups. Four groups need current timetable/identity evidence; Shelfords is waiting-list-only. Milton Squirrels lacks times, Over Beavers is unavailable, Duxford non-Beavers are waiting-list-only, and Fulbourn Beavers has conflicting age statements. Addresses from reviewed HAY inventory require section-specific confirmation; its current HTTP route returned 403. No cross-group timetable borrowing.','','Shredder: all six Cambridge-area venue pages reviewed. Seven coaches yield 11 child-facing coach/day drafts. Group buttons request email enquiries; exact times are absent. Private-only Jesus Green and undated holiday offers do not produce occurrences. Operator age 5+ supersedes older directory age 3+. Adult Monday classes are excluded. Unknown-time drafts cannot be marked ready in the console.','','Baby Gym: recovered primary operator table yields seven weekly sessions for ages 9 months+. Duplicate RISE timetable rows are not collected. Only the starred Tuesday 10:30 session is explicitly term-time-only. Venue addresses and £4.50/£4.10 pricing discrepancy need review.','','## Route, place and mobile decisions','','| Record | Evidence-based recommendation | Remaining action |','|---|---|---|']
    for r in cohort['records']:
        if 'source_review' in r:
            v=r['source_review'];lines.append('| '+r['title']+' | '+v['recommendation'].replace('|','/')+' | '+' '.join(v['remaining']).replace('|','/')+' |')
    lines+=['','A 404 alone does not prove closure. Cached past dates are labelled as historical evidence. Curiosity Club is excluded from evidenced child/family supply because its current programme is 50+/55+. Bampton Poetry Special was 30 September; old Didcot Rhymetime was 17 July. Branch discovery pages do not substitute another programme for either historical row. Wildlings has an accessible route but lists May dates, so current availability is unqualified. BAYSE has only a cached past occurrence and a current 404.','','The marble sculpture belongs in place review with primary Berkeley Square evidence; venue matching must precede withdrawal of the activity alias. Total Ballers is mobile/by arrangement; neither the generic Hoop map pin nor daily placeholder time establishes a fixed venue or guaranteed availability. The primary booking hub is retained without making contact or a booking.','','## Interface and evidence','','Open [the local action console](ds10-action-console-2026-10-12.html), refresh, then **Add generated proposals to this draft**. Existing edits are preserved and proposal keys prevent repeated additions. For Baby Gym, choose **Split into individual sessions**. Route/place/mobile reviews show the recommendation and remaining questions. JSON export/import retains cohort/fingerprint validation; ready status remains a human decision. The console is an offline prototype, not the authenticated production operations UI requested in #70.','','Evidence files in `artefacts/data`: `ds10-automated-session-proposals-2026-10-12.json`, the two council snapshots/extractions, GK Fit/Scouts/Shredder extraction ledgers, the Scout route manifest, and `ds10-remaining-source-review-2026-10-12.json`. Their public links, constraints and exclusions remain with proposals. Local full database backups, caches, virtual environments and dependency runtimes are excluded from publication.','','## Verification and operating limits','','**152 Python tests passed**, plus console validation, guarded import tests and both inline JavaScript syntax checks. Tests cover duplicate identities, changed layouts, unsafe links, past/full/ended exclusions, age conflicts, separate colonies/nights, missing times and partial failures. Single-programme replay preserves other parent records. No model calls are used by these deterministic proposal adapters. Per-run limits are 50 network attempts and 36 checked public pages; last-run counters are not cumulative totals. Browser-derived council snapshots are clearly separated from HTTP collection.','','Run one selected programme at a time with `scripts/collect_ds10_session_proposals.py --record-id <record UUID> --as-of 2026-10-12`, then rebuild with `scripts/build_ds10_action_console.py`. The route ledger is attached with `scripts/record_ds10_remaining_source_review.py`. Global request budgets may make a full batch partial; source failures are not proof of absent supply.','','## Acceptance and ticket follow-up','','- **#39:** implementation/proposals and route review delivered; retain human 100-row scoring, current source access, venue/eligibility review, historical decision application, normal worker rollout/repeat ingestion, pilot breadth and seven-day evidence as open.','- **#40:** canonical matching, alias resolution (including Barton and the sculpture), relationship provenance and repeat/concurrent-import checks remain open. Named venues are not approved canonical identities.','- **#70:** offline 19-record prototype and schemas provided; authenticated production operations UI, permissions and all other operational queues remain open.','- **#32:** bounded cost/access evidence provided; scheduled monitoring and seven-day operational observation remain open.','- **#44 / #29:** no release or pilot acceptance claimed. Pilot remains W3 9LN, 10 km, ages 0–5; national/wider-age proposals are not London pilot supply.','- **#38:** closed source-audit baseline remains closed; these implementation/access findings are follow-up evidence under #39.','','All relevant ticket updates link to this report on the draft branch. PR #71 remains draft and unmerged.']
    (ROOT/'artefacts/documentation/ds10-source-completion-summary-2026-10-12.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
    print(json.dumps(dict(records=19,distinct_proposals=distinct,parent_rows=rows,unapproved=True)))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
